From 04731aeba195e6f00e5183b1c98e83cfee7c8009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:37:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08048/11362] The wired induce treatment changes the engine on
 every game and the agent's actions on none

PHASE 3: REFUSE the 12-cell banked-levels grid. Not "too few cells perturb" --
ZERO. Four of four comparable A/B pairs produced BYTE-IDENTICAL action traces
(ft09 27/27, tn36 31/31, vc33 18/18, sc25 27/27). A pair whose arms emit the
same actions cannot differ on any endpoint downstream of those actions, so no
outcome of that grid could reach alpha.

Phase 2 refused the same grid on an analytic bound and left open which of two
channels was real, noting a live pre-flight "picks 16 cells over 68". It bought
something better than a cell count: the answer is NEITHER channel. The treatment
does not reach the endpoint at all, so no grid size licenses it.

Both arms are the same commit, repo, assets and llama-server process, differing
only in two env vars read inside induce(). The treatment arm leaves them UNSET
(the shipped default) rather than re-specifying 1.1, so it would notice a
reverted wiring. Both A/A floors were measured, not argued -- a single floor
witnesses one arm, and this treatment changes the sampler.

THE TREATMENT WAS ACTIVE, proven three ways, so this is not "the flag didn't
apply": the penalty reads back 1.1/1.0 through the shipped accessor; 17 cells
produced 17 DISTINCT engines; and on tn36 the treatment's engine scored held-out
accuracy 1.0 where the control scored 0.0 -- while both arms took byte-identically
the same 31 actions. That last row is the result in one line.

WHERE THE CHAIN BREAKS: n_plans_found is 0 in every completed cell but one. The
only cell whose trace diverged (ft09, ctl vs its OWN replicate) is the only cell
where n_plans_found differed. So actions move when and only when a plan is found,
the treatment never changed that, and run-to-run noise changed it once -- more
than the treatment did. The next target is plan_in_model, not induce-payload
tuning.

THE RE-ASK HALF WAS NEVER EXERCISED: 0 reasks in all 17 cells, because every live
induction passed static validation. Phase 1's 22-of-36 defective-accept rate did
NOT reproduce live. This is "the tier never fired", not "the tier did not help".

Instrument findings: the seed does NOT make induce deterministic (ctl vs ctlb,
same seed/config/code/process, different engine source and on ft09 a different
plan outcome); a server-process guard was added to the scorer after both servers
were replaced mid-session by a concurrent agent, and it excludes tu93 rather than
scoring a confounded pair; and a bug in this harness (no trtb arm) was found and
fixed mid-run, then backfilled.

Do not over-read: 0 of 4-5 is not "never" -- the 95% upper bound on the rate is
0.451, so the refusal rests on the MECHANISM at least as much as the count. A
REFUSE means only that THIS grid cannot produce a finding; Phase 1's induce-level
effect stands.

No flag was changed on the basis of this run. No scored or online ARC game was
played. Nothing was submitted.
